.git
__pycache__
**/__pycache__/
*.md
!README.md
.gitignore
.dockerignore
# Env files at any depth — backend/.env must never be baked into the image
# (a root-only `.env` pattern does NOT match nested paths in .dockerignore)
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.encryption_key
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
# Log files from the dev machine must never be baked into the image. The
# default `log_file` is the RELATIVE path "log/sublarr.log", which resolves to
# /app/log/sublarr.log in the container — so any install that does not set
# SUBLARR_LOG_FILE appends its own lines to whatever shipped there. Images
# built before this rule carried 17 MB of the maintainer's Windows logs, and a
# user's support bundle would have contained them, complete with a foreign
# machine's platform and paths.
log/
**/log/
*.log
**/*.log
Modelfile
scripts/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
**/venv/
**/.venv/
frontend/.vite/
# Local databases, SQLite sidecars/backups, and runtime state at every depth.
# Root-only globs do not exclude backend/instance/dev_local.db.
**/*.db*
**/*.sqlite*
backend/instance/
backend/dev/
config/
dev-media/
test-media/
# Test suites, coverage reports, and development caches are not runtime code.
**/tests/
**/__tests__/
**/htmlcov/
**/coverage/
**/coverage.*
**/.coverage*
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.benchmarks/
**/test-results/
.vscode/
.idea/
SUBLARR-PLAN.md
PLAN.md
